1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,550
I'm an Argentine traveler. I land in São Paulo: no service.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,350
Roaming shows up on next month's bill, and an eSIM pack on my Argentine card

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,570
adds 30% percepción, and whatever I don't use, I lose.

4
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:14,730
eSIMs sell closed packs and keep what you don't use.

5
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:20,380
Many of us save in digital dollars, but nobody returns the unused part to our wallet.

6
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:25,150
AstroAm: pay in USDC, skip the percepción, and get back what you don't use.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:29,090
You deposit USDC once, signing in Phantom,

8
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:31,870
into an escrow program on Solana. Not to us.

9
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:36,030
Scan the QR, and you're online. This demo uses a sample eSIM.

10
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,750
Our meter signs your usage, the Solana program verifies it,

11
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:43,220
and your eSIM tops itself up. No popups.

12
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:47,350
Deposit 10 USDC and use 250 megabytes in Brazil:

13
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:53,630
one close pays 0.625 and sends 9.375 back to your wallet.

14
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:56,070
After 7 days, anyone can close:

15
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:58,990
what you used is paid, the rest comes back.

16
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:02,470
It runs on Solana devnet today, with 22 program tests

17
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:06,630
and one real Citrus eSIM issued from the flow and settled on-chain.

18
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:09,870
We interviewed 10 travelers from Jujuy:

19
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:14,210
half skip mobile data abroad, four already hold digital dollars.

20
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:19,130
Our customers are Argentine travelers to Chile, Brazil and Uruguay.

21
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:22,800
They pay 2.48 USDC per gigabyte used,

22
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:27,270
at least 21% below the cheapest card eSIM,

23
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:30,690
and 60% or more when they use half.

24
00:01:30,740 --> 00:01:33,930
We keep 0.83 per gigabyte.

25
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:36,870
Our first channel: travel agencies in Jujuy.

26
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:40,630
We are 4 builders from Jujuy. Franco: escrow program and backend.

27
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:45,810
Ignacio: eSIM connectivity. Daniel: metering and the interviews. Joel: the app.

28
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:48,820
We live next to the border. We are the travelers.

29
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:54,230
Next: 10 real trips with Argentine travelers, a Squads multisig, then mainnet.

30
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:58,020
AstroAm. Travel connected. Pay only for what you use.
